  "notes": "Can be written as either {嘆|なげ}く or {歎|なげ}く, though the first is far more common. Used both for personal grief and for deploring social trends or conditions. Has a literary quality and is often seen in written text.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- ⟦{運命|うんめい}→運命：06879_unmei⟧⟦を→を：00422_wo⟧{嘆|なげ}く: to lament one's fate\n- ⟦{死|し}→死：13248_shi⟧⟦を→を：00422_wo⟧{嘆|なげ}く: to mourn a death\n- {嘆|なげ}き{悲|かな}しむ: to grieve and sorrow\n- ⟦{世|よ}→世：00424_yo⟧⟦を→を：00422_wo⟧{嘆|なげ}く: to lament the state of the world",
